One embedded SQL string mixing Oracle and SQL Server idioms
(diag.sql_dialect_mix, info tier): NVL and SYSDATE beside GETDATE and
ISNULL. The message names the markers on each side.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Recent;
	:DECLARE aRows;
	aRows := SQLExecute("SELECT ordno, NVL(status, 'X'), ISNULL(kind, 'Y') FROM orders WHERE logdate > GETDATE() - 1 OR duedate < SYSDATE");
	:RETURN aRows;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Recent;
	:DECLARE aRows;
	aRows := SQLExecute("
	    SELECT ordno, NVL(status, 'X'), ISNULL(kind, 'Y')
	    FROM orders
	    WHERE logdate > GETDATE() - 1
	      OR duedate < SYSDATE
	");
	:RETURN aRows;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:22-3:136 info sql_dialect_mix: Oracle-only (NVL, SYSDATE) and SQL Server-only (ISNULL, GETDATE) idioms in one statement - STARLIMS environments run one dialect, so one side of this will fail there
